Description: Liquid-glass shell of Aegis OS (panel, dock, Dynamic Island, Control Center, Launcher)
 Aegis Shell is the Qt Quick 6 shell of Aegis OS, running on KWin 6 Wayland
 through the layer-shell protocol. Surfaces: a 28 px glass top panel, the
 floating liquid-glass dock with macOS-grade magnification (clamped linear
 map, spring mass 0.1 / stiffness 170 / damping 13, two Euler substeps), the
 120x4 sliver, and the Dynamic Island live-activity capsule (idle 104x32,
 spring mass 1 / stiffness 420 / damping 28).
 .
 M2 surfaces: the 348 px Control Center sheet (Wi-Fi / Bluetooth / Calm /
 Dark tiles, Do Not Disturb, Display + Sound sliders, the live tier badge
 wired to the adaptive effects governor), the full-screen Launcher (8x3
 glass grid, type-to-filter), notification banners (356x84, stack <= 3,
 org.freedesktop.Notifications compatible), and the lock screen (118 px
 thin clock, PAM unlock through the setuid aegis-auth helper).
 .
 The adaptive effects governor (proposal Listing 2) demotes the session
 tier A->B->C on sustained frame times and battery, and exposes the live
 tier on org.aegis.Governor; applications publish island activities via
 org.aegis.Island (see docs/LIVE-ACTIVITY-API.md).
 .
 Design tokens are code: shell/src/qml/Tokens.qml mirrors the tables of the
 Aegis OS UI design proposal v1.3 (+ the v1.4 island override).
